live Instance: api, worker, web, postgres, lemonade, honcho running from 09:03:34; its supervisor (same
  /var/run/docker.sock bind from the distro) was found recreated at 09:05:03, not restarted in place
09:10:56 rakazo-c+ rules: v4 0 (INPUT 0), v6 0     <- no sidecar, no rules; Docker never retried the failed starts
=> the sidecar did not come back. Fail closed held only because the test supervisor failed the same way.

## Where the mounts come from (containers started from each CLI, /proc/<pid>/mountinfo root of /var/run/docker.sock)
started from Windows' docker.exe:   root=/host-services/docker.proxy.sock   (Docker Desktop's own proxy, inside its VM)
started from the WSL distro:        root=/docker.sock under docker-desktop-bind-mounts/Ubuntu (the distro's socket)
Bind-mounted files from a WSL path are likewise served from docker-desktop-bind-mounts/<distro>/…, which exists only
while that distro is running and Docker Desktop's integration has attached it.

